"""Repack a scanned PDF at a fraction of its size, keeping the text sharp.

Pages are classified by content and each class is encoded with the codec that
suits it: bitonal text goes to JBIG2, greyscale pictures to greyscale JPEG,
and anything carrying colour to MRC (a JBIG2 text mask over a JPEG2000 colour
background). The result is reassembled in page order and wrapped as PDF/A
without re-encoding.

See docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-30-pdf-compression-implementation-spec.md
for the measurements behind the defaults.

External programs required: pdftoppm (poppler), tesseract, ocrmypdf,
grk_compress (grok). recode_pdf is installed automatically as a dependency.
"""
